  "notes": "{奪|うば}う is a godan verb meaning 'to snatch,' 'to rob,' or 'to take by force.' It implies forceful or aggressive taking, often against someone's will.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- {奪|うば}う is transitive (takes a direct object)\n- Passive: {奪|うば}われる (to have something taken/snatched)\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {命|いのち}を{奪|うば}う: to take someone's life\n- {目|め}を{奪|うば}う: to captivate (literally 'steal one's eyes')\n- {心|こころ}を{奪|うば}う: to steal someone's heart\n- {自由|じゆう}を{奪|うば}う: to take away freedom\n- {時間|じかん}を{奪|うば}う: to take up someone's time\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {盗|ぬす}む: to steal (secretly, covertly)\n- {取|と}る: to take (neutral)\n- {強奪|ごうだつ}する: to rob (formal/literary)",
